{
  "format": "srwb",
  "version": "1.0",
  "notebook": {
    "name": "円周率の計算: アルキメデスの上下界",
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "# アルキメデスの上下界による円周率の計算\n\nアルキメデスは、円に内接および外接する多角形の周長によって円周率（$\\pi$）を上下から挟み込みました。このワークブックでは、数値的な漸化式に円周率の値を直接代入することなく、同じ考え方を用います。単位円に内接・外接する正六角形から開始し、辺の数を繰り返し2倍に増やしながら、円周率を下界と上界で挟み込んでいきます。\n\n最初のプロットは、幾何学的な位置関係を視覚化するためにのみ三角関数を使用しています。その後に続く上下界の計算では、平方根と直前の多角形の辺長のみを使用します。",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "import numpy as np\n\n# Visualize the starting hexagon inside a unit circle.\ntheta = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, 200)\nangles = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, 6, endpoint=False)\nx_hex = np.r_[np.cos(angles), np.cos(angles[0])]\ny_hex = np.r_[np.sin(angles), np.sin(angles[0])]\n\ncircle = {\"x\": np.cos(theta), \"y\": np.sin(theta), \"mode\": \"lines\", \"name\": \"Unit circle\"}\nhexagon = {\"x\": x_hex, \"y\": y_hex, \"mode\": \"lines+markers\", \"name\": \"Inscribed hexagon\"}\nlayout = {\"title\": \"Archimedes starts with a hexagon\", \"xaxis\": {\"scaleanchor\": \"y\"}, \"yaxis\": {\"scaleanchor\": \"x\"}}\nmplot([circle, hexagon], layout=layout)",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "geometry"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "import math\n\ndef archimedes_rows(doublings=16):\n    \"\"\"Return rigorous polygon bounds for a unit circle.\n\n    chord is the side length of the inscribed n-gon. The stable half-angle\n    recurrence doubles n without requiring pi.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = 6\n    chord = 1.0\n    rows = []\n    for step in range(doublings + 1):\n        half_chord = chord / 2\n        lower = n * half_chord\n        upper = n * half_chord / math.sqrt(1 - half_chord * half_chord)\n        rows.append((step, n, lower, upper, upper - lower))\n        chord = chord / math.sqrt(2 + math.sqrt(4 - chord * chord))\n        n *= 2\n    return rows\n\nrows = archimedes_rows()\nprint(f\"{'step':>4} {'sides':>9} {'lower bound':>16} {'upper bound':>16} {'width':>12}\")\nfor step, n, lower, upper, width in rows:\n    if step in {0, 1, 2, 4, 7, 10, 13, 16}:\n        print(f\"{step:>4} {n:>9,} {lower:>16.12f} {upper:>16.12f} {width:>12.2e}\")\n\nlower, upper = rows[-1][2], rows[-1][3]\nprint(f\"\\nFinal enclosure: {lower:.12f} < pi < {upper:.12f}\")",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "bounds"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "# How many sides are needed before the complete enclosure is narrower\n# than 10^-d? Values are for repeated doubling from the hexagon.\nfirst_for_digits = {}\nfor step, n, lower, upper, width in archimedes_rows(22):\n    for d in range(1, 11):\n        if d not in first_for_digits and width < 10 ** (-d):\n            first_for_digits[d] = (n, width)\n\nprint(f\"{'d':>3} {'first doubled n':>18} {'bound width':>14}\")\nfor d in range(1, 11):\n    n, width = first_for_digits[d]\n    print(f\"{d:>3} {n:>18,} {width:>14.2e}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nA narrower enclosure certifies more absolute accuracy; it is stronger\")\nprint(\"than merely counting matching digits in one floating-point approximation.\")",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "accuracy"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "import sympy as sp\n\nn = sp.symbols('n', positive=True)\ninscribed_area = (n / 2) * sp.sin(2 * sp.pi / n)\nlimit_value = sp.limit(inscribed_area, n, sp.oo)\n\nprint(\"Symbolic check of the familiar inscribed-area formula:\")\nprint(\"limit as n approaches infinity =\", limit_value)\nassert limit_value == sp.pi\ninscribed_area",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "symbolic_limit"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "def leibniz_terms_for_error(d):\n    # Alternating-series remainder for pi is at most 4/(2N+1).\n    return math.ceil((4 * 10**d - 1) / 2)\n\ndef arctan_series(x, terms):\n    return sum((-1)**k * x**(2*k + 1) / (2*k + 1) for k in range(terms))\n\ndef machin_pi(terms):\n    return 4 * (4 * arctan_series(1/5, terms) - arctan_series(1/239, terms))\n\nmachin_terms = next(n for n in range(1, 30) if abs(machin_pi(n) - math.pi) < 1e-10)\npolygon_sides, polygon_width = first_for_digits[10]\n\nprint(\"Work needed for about 1e-10 absolute accuracy:\")\nprint(f\"  Leibniz guarantee:       {leibniz_terms_for_error(10):,} terms\")\nprint(f\"  Polygon bound width:     {polygon_sides:,} sides (width {polygon_width:.2e})\")\nprint(f\"  Machin formula in float: {machin_terms} terms per arctangent\")\nprint(\"\\nThe methods have very different convergence rates; the polygon method's\")\nprint(\"historical importance is its rigorous geometric squeeze, not raw speed.\")",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "comparison"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "## まとめ（キーポイント）\n\n- 数値的な漸化式は既知の六角形の辺長から開始し、円周率の数値的な値を事前には仮定しません。\n- 各反復ごとに下界と上界の両方が得られます。\n- 辺の数を2倍にするごとに、挟み込みの幅（誤差範囲）はおよそ4分の1に減少します。\n- 記号極限は収束の理由を説明するものであり、それ自体が数値計算アルゴリズムではありません。\n- 厳密な誤差限界（error bound）を持つことは、浮動小数点数の参照値とたまたま一致する桁数を数えることとは本質的に異なります。",
        "language": "markdown"
      }
    ]
  }
}
